    <div class="section-head measure">
      <p class="eyebrow">The part most apps skip</p>
      <h2>We tell you which routes have actually been ridden.</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft)">A route drawn from a map and a route someone has ridden on a horse are not the same thing, and you deserve to know which one you&rsquo;re about to load a horse for. Every route in BridleNav carries a badge.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tier t-ver">
      <div class="count">12</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Verified</h3>
        <p>Personally ridden and checked by BridleNav or a trusted local guide.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier t-doc">
      <div class="count">2</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Documented</h3>
        <p>Based on a local rider&rsquo;s detailed guide, but not yet personally ridden by the BridleNav team.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier t-plo">
      <div class="count">27</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Map-plotted</h3>
        <p>Drawn from maps, not yet ridden. Full written guide, parking and notes &mdash; but no spoken turn-by-turn yet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier t-com">
      <div class="count">&mdash;</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Shared by a rider</h3>
        <p>Recorded and written up by another rider, and read by us before it went live. Not ridden by the BridleNav team, and we say so on the route.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px;color:var(--ink-soft);max-width:34rem">Forty-one routes to begin with, every one badged honestly. If nobody has ridden it yet, we say so.</p>
  </div>
</section>

